> Inspect the exact degree masks before fitting

Even blocks assign input degrees (1,2); odd blocks use (2,1). Hidden unit j
has degree floor(j/8): eight constant units of degree 0 and eight of degree 1.
The four output degrees repeat the input pair. A hidden edge is allowed when
input_degree<=hidden_degree; a head edge requires **hidden_degree<head_degree**.
The strict final comparison excludes own and later input paths. A degree 0
hidden unit can still contribute a constant through its bias.

The panels show every entry of both masks for both distinct orders. Blue means
an allowed edge; white means blocked. Axis positions are raw input, hidden or
head indices, with head order mu0,mu1,raw_s0,raw_s1. There are24 blocked hidden
kernel entries and16 blocked head entries per block:40 of 96 kernel entries.
All remain stored model parameters; their zero partials follow from structural
mask multiplication inside the graph. With initially zero Adam moments, all 160
forbidden kernel values across four blocks remain unchanged throughout fitting.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/iaf_masks.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{255,255,255},{37,99,235}};
 auto panel=[&](const n::Tensor& mask,const std::string& title,bool output){
  auto values=mask.to_vector<double>();int incoming=mask.size(0),outgoing=mask.size(1);
  std::vector<double> x(outgoing),y(incoming);std::vector<std::vector<double>> z(outgoing,std::vector<double>(incoming));
  for(int j=0;j<outgoing;++j){x[j]=j;for(int i=0;i<incoming;++i)z[j][i]=values[i*outgoing+j];}
  for(int i=0;i<incoming;++i)y[i]=i;
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.image(x,y,z,colors,0,1)
  .x_limits(-.5,outgoing-.5).y_limits(-.5,incoming-.5).margins(75,22,58,68)
  .x_label(output?"Head index: mu0,mu1,raw_s0,raw_s1":"Hidden unit index")
  .y_label(output?"Hidden unit index":"Raw input coordinate").title(title);
  if(output)p.x_ticks({0,1,2,3},{"mu0","mu1","raw_s0","raw_s1"}).y_ticks({0,4,8,12,15},{"0","4","8","12","15"});
  else p.x_ticks({0,4,8,12,15},{"0","4","8","12","15"}).y_ticks({0,1},{"0","1"});
  return p;
 };
 auto even=n::models::MafMasks(0),odd=n::models::MafMasks(1);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2,2)
 .add(panel(even.input_mask,"Even order0,1: input <= hidden",false))
 .add(panel(even.output_mask,"Even order0,1: hidden < head",true))
 .add(panel(odd.input_mask,"Odd order1,0: input <= hidden",false))
 .add(panel(odd.output_mask,"Odd order1,0: hidden < head",true))
 .size(1100,900).fit_panels().save_svg("build/iaf_masks.svg");
 std::print("Two distinct strict orders; all192 displayed mask entries retained. Forty forbidden kernel coordinates per block,160 across four blocks.\n");
}
